From seedds/nxnative (MIT), its Ryujinx changes for geometry shaders as Metal compute kernels: bb585cd5 (the fixed
144-word vertex capture input, IGpuAccessor.QueryGeometryInputFixed / ResourceReservations.FillGeometryInputMap),
31b5944e and 2c31212f (explicit passthrough vertices with every captured attribute, the output primitive of a
passthrough shader from its input topology, empty strips not ended, at most MaxOutputVertices emitted, viewport-mask
culling of a passthrough primitive, a 32x1x1 thread group) and 364e86a1 (draw-wide primitive IDs across split
dispatches: vb_info.geometry_counts.y is the dispatch's first primitive). Every change is behind
QueryGeometryInputFixed() or a geometry stage, so vertex, pixel and compute translations are unchanged.


